      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The dermatoglyphic studies showing the existence of genetic predisposition to the development of coronary heart disease were conducted. Methods based on the mathematical theory of pattern recognition were used for multifactorial analysis of the material. It was established that complex evaluation of 20 dermatoglyphic parameters could be reliable in predicting genetic risk factor in the development of this cardiovascular pathology."},
